          'content': 'BASICS:\n% means \'per hundred\' — out of 100\nx% = x/100\n\nFUNDAMENTAL FORMULAS:\n1. x% of y = (x × y)/100\n2. What % is A of B? = (A/B) × 100\n3. % increase = [(New-Old)/Old] × 100\n4. % decrease = [(Old-New)/Old] × 100\n\nFRACTION-PERCENTAGE TABLE (Must Memorize):\n1/2 = 50%      1/3 = 33.33%    1/4 = 25%\n1/5 = 20%      1/6 = 16.67%    1/7 = 14.28%\n1/8 = 12.5%    1/9 = 11.11%    1/10 = 10%\n1/11 = 9.09%   1/12 = 8.33%    1/20 = 5%\n1/25 = 4%      1/50 = 2%       1/100 = 1%\n\n2/3 = 66.67%   3/4 = 75%       2/5 = 40%\n3/5 = 60%      4/5 = 80%       5/6 = 83.33%\n\nSUCCESSIVE PERCENTAGE CHANGE:\nIf a value increases by A% then by B%:\nNet change = A + B + (A×B)/100\n\nIf increase: +A%, if decrease: -A%\n\nExample 1: Price increases 10% then decreases 10%\nNet = 10 + (-10) + (10×(-10))/100 = 0 - 1 = -1%\nSo final price is 1% LESS (not same!)\n\nExample 2: Salary increases 20% then 15%\nNet = 20 + 15 + (20×15)/100 = 35 + 3 = 38% increase\n\nBACK CALCULATION:\nIf final value after x% increase = Final\nOriginal = Final × 100/(100+x)\n\nIf final value after x% decrease = Final\nOriginal = Final × 100/(100-x)\n\nExample: After 20% increase price is ₹360. Find original.\nOriginal = 360 × 100/120 = ₹300\n\nPOPULATION FORMULA:\nPopulation after n years = P × (1 + r/100)^n\nIf growth rate changes each year:\nP_final = P × (1+r1/100) × (1+r2/100) × (1+r3/100)\n\nINGREDIENT MIXTURE:\nIf A% solution and B% solution mixed in ratio m:n:\nResult = (A×m + B×n)/(m+n)%\n\nCOMMON TRAPS:\n1. \'25% more than\' ≠ \'25% of\'\n   \'25% more than 80\' = 80 + 25% of 80 = 80 + 20 = 100\n2. Percentage increase and decrease are NOT equal in opposite directions\n   +25% then -25% gives net = -6.25% (not 0)\n3. Always check: % of WHAT? (base value matters)\n\nSPEED CALCULATION TIPS:\n• To find 15% of N: find 10% + 5% = N/10 + N/20\n• To find 12.5% of N: N/8\n• To find 37.5% of N: 3N/8\n• To find 66.67% of N: 2N/3',
