          'content': 'BASIC CONCEPT:\nIf A can complete work in \'n\' days:\nA\'s 1 day work = 1/n of total work\n\nLCM METHOD (Fastest for SSC):\n1. Take LCM of all given days as \'Total Work\' (in units)\n2. Find each person\'s work per day = Total/Their days\n3. Add efficiencies for combined work\n4. Time = Total Work / Combined efficiency\n\nExample: A completes in 12 days, B in 15 days\nLCM(12,15) = 60 units\nA\'s efficiency = 60/12 = 5 units/day\nB\'s efficiency = 60/15 = 4 units/day\nTogether = 9 units/day\nTime = 60/9 = 6.67 days\n\nFORMULA METHOD:\nA and B together = ab/(a+b) days\nA, B, C together = abc/(ab+bc+ca) days\n\nWORK WITH WAGES:\nWages distributed in RATIO OF WORK DONE\n(Not in ratio of number of days worked)\n\nExample: A works 5 days, B works 3 days on same job\nA\'s efficiency = 1/10 per day, B\'s = 1/15 per day\nWork by A = 5 × 1/10 = 1/2\nWork by B = 3 × 1/15 = 1/5\nRatio A:B = 1/2 : 1/5 = 5:2\nIf total wages = ₹700, A gets ₹500, B gets ₹200\n\nPIPES AND CISTERNS:\nInlet pipe: fills tank (+positive)\nOutlet pipe (leak): empties tank (-negative)\nNet rate = (Sum of inlet rates) - (Sum of outlet rates)\n\nExample: Inlet fills in 6 hours, outlet empties in 10 hours\nNet rate = 1/6 - 1/10 = 5/30 - 3/30 = 2/30 = 1/15 per hour\nTank fills in 15 hours\n\nMDH FORMULA (MEN-DAYS-HOURS):\nM₁ × D₁ × H₁ / W₁ = M₂ × D₂ × H₂ / W₂\n\nExample: 8 men finish work in 12 days working 6 hours/day.\nHow many days for 12 men working 8 hours/day for same work?\n8×12×6/1 = 12×D×8/1\nD = 8×12×6/(12×8) = 6 days\n\nA DOES PART, B FINISHES:\nA works for x days, then B alone finishes in y days\nTotal work = (x × A\'s efficiency) + (y × B\'s efficiency) = 1\n\nMAN-WOMAN-CHILD PROBLEMS:\nIf given: 1 man = n women = m children (efficiency)\nConvert all to same unit and solve using MDH formula\n\nCYCLIC WORK:\n(A+B) work on day 1, (B+C) work on day 2, pattern repeats\nFind work per cycle (2 days here), then find total cycles',
