          'weightage': '3-4 questions',
          'difficulty': 'Medium',
          'readTime': '15 mins',
          'content': 'FUNDAMENTAL FORMULA:\nSpeed = Distance / Time\nDistance = Speed × Time\nTime = Distance / Speed\n\nUNIT CONVERSIONS:\n1 km/h = 5/18 m/s [multiply by 5/18 to convert km/h to m/s]\n1 m/s = 18/5 km/h [multiply by 18/5 to convert m/s to km/h]\n\nMemory trick: 18/5 = 3.6\nSo 10 m/s = 36 km/h, 5 m/s = 18 km/h\n\nAVERAGE SPEED:\nIf same DISTANCE covered at speeds S1 and S2:\nAverage speed = 2S1S2/(S1+S2) [Harmonic mean]\n\n⚠️ Average speed ≠ (S1+S2)/2 when distances are equal\n(S1+S2)/2 is correct ONLY when TIMES are equal\n\nExample: Goes 60km at 30km/h and returns at 20km/h\nAverage speed = 2×30×20/(30+20) = 1200/50 = 24 km/h\n\nRELATIVE SPEED:\nSame direction: Relative speed = |S1 - S2| [subtract]\nOpposite direction: Relative speed = S1 + S2 [add]\n\nTRAIN PROBLEMS:\nPassing a stationary pole/person: Distance = Length of train\nPassing a stationary platform/bridge: Distance = Length of train + Length of platform\nPassing a moving person/train (opposite): Distance = Sum of lengths, Speed = Sum of speeds\nPassing a moving person/train (same direction): Distance = Sum of lengths, Speed = Difference of speeds\n\nTime to cross = Total distance / Relative speed\n\nBOAT AND STREAM:\nLet boat speed in still water = B, Stream speed = S\nDownstream speed (with current) = B + S\nUpstream speed (against current) = B - S\n\nFinding B and S:\nBoat speed B = (Downstream + Upstream)/2\nStream speed S = (Downstream - Upstream)/2\n\nTIME AND DISTANCE FOR MEETINGS:\nTwo persons A and B start from P and Q towards each other:\nTime to meet = Distance PQ / (Speed A + Speed B)\n\nAfter meeting, time for A to reach Q × Time for B to reach P = (Time to meet)²\nUseful: If they meet after t hours, A takes t1 more hours to complete, B takes t2 more:\nt = √(t1 × t2)\n\nCIRCULAR TRACK:\nTwo persons on circular track of length L:\nSame direction - Time to meet again = L / (S1 - S2)\nOpposite direction - Time to meet = L / (S1 + S2)',
