ugh, Painstaking\n• Nefarious = Wicked, Criminal, Villainous\n• Obstinate = Stubborn, Persistent, Headstrong\n• Ominous = Threatening, Foreboding, Menacing\n• Opulent = Wealthy, Affluent, Luxurious\n• Pernicious = Harmful, Destructive, Damaging\n• Placid = Calm, Peaceful, Serene\n• Prolific = Productive, Abundant, Fertile\n• Prudent = Wise, Sensible, Judicious\n• Querulous = Complaining, Whining, Peevish\n• Raucous = Loud, Harsh, Noisy\n• Resilient = Strong, Adaptable, Flexible\n• Reticent = Reserved, Silent, Secretive\n• Sagacious = Wise, Shrewd, Astute\n• Tenacious = Persistent, Determined, Firm\n• Turbulent = Stormy, Chaotic, Unstable\n• Ubiquitous = Everywhere, Omnipresent, Pervasive\n• Vacillate = Waver, Hesitate, Fluctuate\n• Verbose = Wordy, Long-winded, Loquacious\n• Vigilant = Watchful, Alert, Attentive\n• Zealous = Passionate, Enthusiastic, Fervent\n\nIMPORTANT ANTONYMS:\n• Abundance ↔ Scarcity/Dearth\n• Benevolent ↔ Malevolent/Malicious\n• Candid ↔ Evasive/Secretive\n• Diligent ↔ Lazy/Indolent\n• Eminent ↔ Obscure/Unknown\n• Frugal ↔ Extravagant/Lavish/Prodigal\n• Gregarious ↔ Introverted/Reserved\n• Haughty ↔ Humble/Modest\n• Impede ↔ Facilitate/Help/Aid\n• Insolent ↔ Respectful/Polite\n• Loquacious ↔ Taciturn/Reticent\n• Magnanimous ↔ Selfish/Mean\n• Meticulous ↔ Careless/Negligent\n• Prudent ↔ Reckless/Imprudent\n• Turbulent ↔ Calm/Peaceful/Serene\n• Verbose ↔ Concise/Laconic/Terse\n• Zealous ↔ Indifferent/Apathetic',
