          'content': 'PHYSICS — KEY CONCEPTS:\n\nNewton\'s Laws of Motion:\n1st Law (Inertia): Body continues in rest/motion unless external force acts\n2nd Law (F=ma): Force = Mass × Acceleration\n3rd Law (Action-Reaction): Every action has equal and opposite reaction\n\nGravitation:\n• Acceleration due to gravity (g) = 9.8 m/s² on Earth surface\n• g decreases as you go up (away from Earth) or towards centre\n• g is MAXIMUM at poles, MINIMUM at equator\n• Gravitational constant G = 6.67 × 10⁻¹¹ Nm²/kg²\n• Moon\'s gravity = 1/6 of Earth\'s gravity\n\nSound:\n• Needs medium to travel (cannot travel in vacuum)\n• Speed in air ≈ 340 m/s at 20°C\n• Speed: solid > liquid > gas\n• Ultrasound: >20,000 Hz (used in SONAR, medical imaging)\n• Infrasound: <20 Hz (used by elephants, whales)\n\nLight:\n• Speed of light = 3 × 10⁸ m/s (in vacuum)\n• Can travel in vacuum\n• Total Internal Reflection: basis of optical fibre, mirage\n• Dispersion: White light splits into VIBGYOR (Violet, Indigo, Blue, Green, Yellow, Orange, Red)\n• Violet light — shortest wavelength, maximum bending\n• Red light — longest wavelength, minimum bending\n\nElectricity:\n• Ohm\'s Law: V = IR (Voltage = Current × Resistance)\n• Resistance in series: R = R1 + R2 + R3...\n• Resistance in parallel: 1/R = 1/R1 + 1/R2...\n• Power: P = VI = I²R = V²/R\n• 1 unit electricity = 1 kWh = 3.6 × 10⁶ J\n\nCHEMISTRY — KEY CONCEPTS:\n\nAtomic Structure:\n• Proton: +ve charge, in nucleus, mass = 1 amu\n• Neutron: neutral, in nucleus, mass = 1 amu\n• Electron: -ve charge, orbit, mass ≈ 0\n• Atomic number = Number of protons\n• Mass number = Protons + Neutrons\n\nChemical Bonds:\n• Ionic bond: Transfer of electrons (Na+Cl- → NaCl, salt)\n• Covalent bond: Sharing of electrons (H2O, CO2)\n• Metallic bond: Free electrons in metals\n\nImportant Chemical Compounds:\n• NaCl = Common salt\n• NaHCO3 = Baking soda (sodium bicarbonate)\n• Na2CO3 = Washing soda\n• H2O2 = Hydrogen peroxide (bleaching agent)\n• CaCO3 = Limestone/chalk/marble\n• Ca(OH)2 = Slaked lime\n• CaO = Quick lime\n• H2SO4 = Sulphuric acid (king of acids)\n• HCl = Hydrochloric acid (also called muriatic acid)\n• HNO3 = Nitric acid\n• NH3 = Ammonia\n\nGases and Properties:\n• Laughing gas: N2O (Nitrous oxide)\n• Tear gas: CS gas or Chlorobenzalmalononitrile\n• Natural gas: Mainly methane (CH4)\n• LPG: Propane + Butane\n• Ozone (O3): Protects from UV rays (stratosphere)\n• CO: Colourless, odourless, POISONOUS (from incomplete combustion)\n• CO2: Greenhouse gas, extinguishes fire, used in fizzy drinks\n\nBIOLOGY — KEY CONCEPTS:\n\nCell:\n• Robert Hooke discovered cell (1665)\n• Cell theory: All living things made of cells (Schleiden & Schwann)\n• Nucleus: \'Brain of cell\', contains DNA\n• Mitochondria: \'Powerhouse of cell\' (produces energy/ATP)\n• Chloroplast: In plants, site of photosynthesis\n• Ribosome: Site of protein synthesis\n\nHuman Body Systems:\n\nDigestive System:\n• Longest organ: Small intestine (7m)\n• Largest gland: Liver\n• Bile produced by: Liver, stored in Gall bladder\n• Starch digestion begins: Mouth (salivary amylase)\n• Protein digestion begins: Stomach (pepsin)\n\nCirculatory System:\n• Heart: 4 chambers (2 atria + 2 ventricles)\n• Blood cells: RBC (carry oxygen), WBC (fight infection), Platelets (clotting)\n• Blood types: A, B, AB, O\n• Universal donor: O- | Universal recipient: AB+\n• Normal BP: 120/80 mm Hg\n• Heart rate: 72 beats/minute (average)\n\nRespiratory System:\n• Gas exchange in: Alveoli\n• Haemoglobin: Carries oxygen in blood\n• Breathing rate: 15-20 times/minute\n\nNervous System:\n• Neurons: Basic unit of nervous system\n• Brain: 3 parts — Cerebrum (thinking), Cerebellum (balance), Brain stem (involuntary)\n• Spinal cord: Reflex actions\n\nDiseases:\n• Malaria: Plasmodium parasite, Anopheles mosquito, treated with quinine\n• Dengue: Aedes mosquito, viral\n• Tuberculosis (TB): Mycobacterium tuberculosis bacteria\n• AIDS: HIV virus, destroys immune system\n• Rabies: Virus, spreads through dog/bat bite\n• Cholera: Vibrio cholerae bacteria, contaminated water\n• Scurvy: Vitamin C deficiency\n• Rickets: Vitamin D deficiency\n• Night blindness: Vitamin A deficiency\n• Anaemia: Iron deficiency\n\nVITAMINS:\n• Vitamin A: Night vision, deficiency = night blindness\n• Vitamin B complex: B1(thiamine), B2(riboflavin), B3(niacin), B12\n• Vitamin C: Citrus fruits, deficiency = scurvy\n• Vitamin D: Sunshine vitamin, bones, deficiency = rickets\n• Vitamin E: Antioxidant\n• Vitamin K: Blood clotting, deficiency = haemophilia-like symptoms\n• Fat soluble: A, D, E, K\n• Water soluble: B complex, C',
